FINDING A: no "insert-sps-pps" property exists on this NVIDIA nvv4l2h264enc build at all.
That property name belongs to other GStreamer H.264 encoders (e.g. x264enc), not NVIDIA's
hardware V4L2 encoder element. It cannot be set here because it does not exist on this element.

FINDING B: idrinterval (default 256 frames, ~10.4s at 24.7fps) is a DISTINCT property from
iframeinterval (which our code sets to output_fps=30, i.e. ~1.2s). Our code sets iframeinterval
only, not idrinterval. Empirically (Step 3, prior validation round) a fresh real RTSP client join
decoded correctly within the test window, which is direct evidence this combination is
functionally sufficient for GStreamer-based clients that accept in-band SPS/PPS -- but idrinterval
was not independently verified as aligned to iframeinterval.

